2.2. Inclusion criteria
The following outlines the inclusion criteria:
• Articles from peer-reviewed journals, conference proceedings, and book chapters that focus on ML and the IoT applications, and current trends in healthcare. • Studies published between 2020 and 2025 will be included to ensure coverage of recent advancements. • Research articles presenting empirical findings, case studies, or thorough analyses of ML-IoT systems across various healthcare applications • Research published in English and indexed in Scopus or PubMed.
2.3. Exclusion criteria
The exclusion criteria are given below:
• Articles not directly related to healthcare applications of ML or IoT, such as general AI or IoT studies in other industries. • Studies without sufficient methodological details or empirical evidence • Publications older than the past five years. • Non-English articles or those not indexed in reputable databases (Scopus, PubMed) • Duplicate studies or redundant reports with overlapping data.
2.4. Scope
This review indicates recent research on the integration of machine learning (ML) and Internet of Things (IoT) technologies in healthcare, emphasizing applications, emerging trends, and practical implementations. The research studies selected were examined to both summarize recent advancements and to identify trade-offs, challenges, and limitations related to ML–IoT systems. The review offers essential insights into the effectiveness and feasibility of ML–IoT solutions by analyzing various approaches, highlighting best practices, and examining real-world applications. Additionally, it highlights gaps in existing research and suggests potential directions for future studies, with the objective of guiding both scholarly inquiry and evidence-based implementation in clinical environments.
